echnical Design Document (TDD)
Risk Anomaly Detection Dashboard — React Application
Version: 0.1 (draft)
Status: Proposed
Audience: Engineering, product, security operations
Last updated: 2026-06-15

1. Executive summary
This document describes a React-based Risk Anomaly Detection application that gives security and risk teams a single place to:

Monitor total organizational risk score over configurable date ranges
Detect and investigate anomalies in risk signals
Visualize risk concentration via heat maps and breakdown charts
Drill from executive summary → entity detail → evidence
The app is designed as a layered dashboard: scorecards at the top, trend + heatmap in the middle, investigation queue at the bottom, with a dedicated entity detail route for deep dives.

2. Problem statement
Risk data today is fragmented across alerts, entity scores, and time-series metrics. Analysts lack:

A single headline risk number with period-over-period context
A way to see when risk spiked and what drove it
Spatial/temporal heat maps showing concentration by entity, category, and time
A prioritized work queue of anomalies worth investigating
Without this, teams react to individual alerts instead of managing aggregate risk posture.

